From bdd5a4ab6cf55d848fbd194865155ef0d69bcd94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lajosh=C3=A1zi=2C=20L=C3=A1szl=C3=B3=20Gergely?=
 <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:06:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] ASoC: wcd9335: use the shared MBHC implementation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This driver had a jack implementation of its own, written because the
shared one could not be used: it only knew how to detect a plug with an
MBHC ADC, which this codec does not have. With a legacy backend in place
that reason is gone, and what is left is a private implementation that is
strictly weaker than the shared one.

The private code detects a plug and nothing about it. It reports every
insertion as a headphone, because it never measures whether there is a
microphone, and it tracks the direction in a driver-side bool that it flips
on each interrupt - so a single missed or spurious edge inverts the
reported state until the next reboot, which is exactly what was observed.
Buttons were handled here too, with a hand-rolled 120 ms debounce added to
stop the transient at unplug from being reported as a media key press.

The shared implementation answers the question the private one could not:
it separates headphone from headset from line-out from a ground/mic-swapped
plug, and it takes the direction from the codec's own arming bit rather
than from a bool that can drift out of step with it.

The field table is taken from the downstream driver's wcd_mbhc_registers[]
for tasha:

  https://github.com/intervigilium/android_kernel_htc_msm8952
  sound/soc/codecs/wcd9335.c

29 of the shared code's fields, with the ADC, moisture and headphone ground
entries absent - the same list, absence included, that says this codec
belongs on the legacy backend. WCD_MBHC_HPH_CNP_WG_TIME is left out on top
of that: the downstream table has it, but nothing reads it and this
register map does not name the register, so there is nothing to point it at
that could be checked.

The interrupt ids come from the same driver.

Signed-off-by: Lajosházi, László Gergely <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
